          repository has no LICENSE file; LICENSE here is the Apache 2.0 text.

Files:
  alu.sv          upstream src/z8086/alu.sv; two pc10-iii changes (DAA/DAS
                  threshold, NEG byte CF)
  z86_eu.sv       derived from upstream src/z8086/z8086.sv (pc10-iii changes
                  marked "pc10-iii", see its header): the EU without z8086's
                  bus and queue, for biu88, with a clock enable; without
                  z8086's group decode, translation and address-compression
                  logic (see below)
  z86_tables.sv   pc10-iii: the four Intel tables as RAMs (not from z8086)
  z86_overlay.svh pc10-iii: the 8088 interrupt overlay for an 8086 ROM
  cpu_z86.sv      pc10-iii: z86_eu + tables + adapter + biu88 (not from z8086)

Not included (AGENTS.md rule 4: no table from Intel's die in the repository or
in the bitstream):
  - upstream src/z8086/ucode.hex, the 512 x 21-bit 8086 microcode ROM
    (Andrew Jenner's extraction from Ken Shirriff's die photo);
  - the tables that upstream z8086.sv carries as logic: the group decode ROM
    (Shirriff's transcription), the translation ROM entries and the microcode
    address decoder ("uaddr_pack").
All four come from the microcode bundle the user builds with tools/mkucode.py
from his own copy of Jenner's public archive (8086_microcode_v2.zip; it has
the 8088 ROM too) and is loaded at start-up (doc/z8086.md). Upstream z8086.sv
itself was removed from this repository on 2026-10-22 for that reason; the
commit above is the reference.
